. * `estimates save <file>` saves the ACTIVE estimates, not a named one, so make
. * each stored set active with `estimates restore` before saving it.
. estimates restore m1
{txt}(results {stata estimates replay m1:m1} are active now)

{com}. estimates save "output/intermediates/estimates/m1.ster", replace
{res}{txt}(note: file output/intermediates/estimates/m1.ster not found)
{txt}file output/intermediates/estimates/m1.ster saved

{com}. estimates restore m2
{txt}(results {stata estimates replay m2:m2} are active now)

{com}. estimates save "output/intermediates/estimates/m2.ster", replace
{res}{txt}file output/intermediates/estimates/m2.ster saved

{com}. estimates restore m3
{txt}(results {stata estimates replay m3:m3} are active now)

{com}. estimates save "output/intermediates/estimates/m3.ster", replace
{res}{txt}file output/intermediates/estimates/m3.ster saved

{com}. estimates restore m4
{txt}(results {stata estimates replay m4:m4} are active now)

{com}. estimates save "output/intermediates/estimates/m4.ster", replace
{res}{txt}(note: file output/intermediates/estimates/m4.ster not found)
{txt}file output/intermediates/estimates/m4.ster saved

{com}. 
. * Coefficient summary for the Python coefficient plot. paramcode 1 = hydro
. * share, 2 = drought; m4 contributes both coefficients.
. matrix M = (1, 1, `b1', `s1' \ 2, 1, `b2', `s2' \ 3, 2, `b3', `s3' \ 4, 1, `b4', `s4' \ 4, 2, `b4d', `s4d')
{txt}
{com}. matrix colnames M = spec paramcode b se
{txt}
{com}. svmat M, names(col)
{txt}
{com}. keep if !missing(spec)
{txt}(615 observations deleted)

{com}. gen str1 param = "h"
{txt}
{com}. replace param = "d" if paramcode == 2
{txt}(2 real changes made)

{com}. export delimited spec param b se using "output/intermediates/coefs.csv", replace
{res}{txt}(note: file output/intermediates/coefs.csv not found)
{txt}file output/intermediates/coefs.csv saved

{com}. 
